{
  "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
  "version": 1,
  "game": "sshtl_l7",
  "notes": "Williams System 9 diagnostics per the Space Shuttle instruction manual p13: Manual-Down (public -6 = 0) plus Advance (public -7) enters the display test; Auto-Up then Advance steps Test 00 (sound), 01 (lamps) and 02 (solenoids), each shown in the credits display. Manual-Down in Test 02 holds one step, which the ROM pulses while the match display shows its number; each further Advance moves to the next step. Twenty-six Advances show where the sequence ends and wraps. Direct switch writes only, so PinMAME keyboard handling stays off. Run from an NVRAM initialized by one prior empty-NVRAM power-up.",
